  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the bustling city of New York, where skyscrapers touch the clouds and traffic never stops, there's a hidden gem that defies all expectations. The High Line, an elevated park constructed on an abandoned railway line, has become a symbol of urban renaissance.\\\\\nThe project started in 2006 when the city government decided to transform the unused tracks into a pedestrian and bicycle path. Over ten years later, it has grown from an idea into one of the most renowned urban parks in the world.\\\\\nThe High Line is not just about nature; it's also a testament to human ingenuity and resilience. The park features over 100,000 plants, from ornamental trees to vibrant flowers, creating a lush environment that contrasts with the city's harsh realities below.\\\\\nThe High Line has become more than just an outdoor space; it's a hub for art and culture. Various installations, from sculptures to performance spaces, make the walk along the tracks an experience unlike any other.\\\\\nThe park has also become a symbol of community engagement. Local residents have played a crucial role in its development and maintenance, turning what was once a neglected space into a prideful part of their city.\"\n  },\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the original purpose of the High Line?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) A railway line for passenger transport\",\n        \"B) An outdoor art gallery\",\n        \"C) A pedestrian and bicycle path\",\n        \"D) A residential apartment building\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is the High Line not known for?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) A hidden gem in New York City\",\n        \"B) An urban park on an abandoned railway line\",\n        \"C) A hub for art and culture\",\n        \"D) A residential apartment building\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following best describes the High Line's contribution to urban renaissance?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) It preserves historical buildings\",\n        \"B) It transforms abandoned spaces into green areas\",\n        \"C) It encourages residential development\",\n        \"D) It promotes industrial activities\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What role have local residents played in the High Line's development?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) They were primarily financial backers\",\n        \"B) They only participated in maintenance work\",\n        \"C) They have been actively engaged in the project from start to finish\",\n        \"D) They were not involved at all\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the High Line's most significant contribution to New York City?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) It has reduced traffic congestion\",\n        \"B) It has created a green space in the midst of urban sprawl\",\n        \"C) It has attracted tourists from around the world\",\n        \"D) It has improved public transportation\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
